## 6. What the Tech Specs Agent Achieves

### For the User

| Output Section | What It Delivers |
|:---|:---|
| **System Overview** | High-level architecture pattern, key design decisions |
| **Data Model** | Entity definitions, fields, relationships (ERD-ready) |
| **API Design** | REST endpoints with methods, paths, request/response bodies |
| **Component Breakdown** | Modules, their responsibilities, and dependencies |
| **Non-Functional Reqs** | Performance, security, scalability, availability targets |
| **Tech Stack** | Recommended frontend, backend, database, infrastructure |
| **Risks & Mitigations** | Identified risks with impact analysis and mitigation plans |
| **Open Questions** | Items needing stakeholder clarification |

### For the SDLC Pipeline

- Bridges the gap between **"What to build"** (user stories) and **"How to build it"** (engineering blueprint)
- Produces a **structured, version-controlled artifact** uploaded to GitHub alongside the user stories
- Enables downstream agents (WBS generation, code scaffolding, test plan generation) to consume a well-defined schema

